            0.119
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Q9. Fill a table such that the cell having the second largest number is not a supercell but the second smallest number is a supercell. Is it possible?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.128,
            0.341,
            0.145
          ],
          "content": "Ans. One of the ways is-"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.154,
            0.391,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": "Second smallest number a super cell"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.412,
            0.167,
            0.672,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "| 2 | 1 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 7 | 9 | 8 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_22_table_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.684,
            0.153,
            0.886,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "Second largest number 8 is not a supercell."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.229,
            0.748,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": "**Q10. Make other variations of this puzzle and challenge your classmates.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.255,
            0.366,
            0.271
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Some of these could be-"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.273,
            0.792,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": "Can you fill the table with 9 cells such that there are more than 5 super cells? Can you fill the table with 9 cells such that there are exactly 4 super cells?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.343,
            0.226,
            0.361
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Page No. 58"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.369,
            0.883,
            0.419
          ],
          "content": "**Q. Complete Table 2 with 5-digit numbers whose digits are ‘1’, ‘0’, ‘6’, ‘3’, and ‘9’ in some order. Only a coloured cell should have a number greater than all its neighbours.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.428,
            0.393,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Table 2 (One of the ways) –"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.451,
            0.484,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": "| 96,310 | 96,301 | 36,109 | 39,160 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 96,103 | 13,609 | 60,319 | 19,306 |\n| 13,906 | 10,396 | 60,193 | 60,931 |\n| 10,369 | 10,963 | 10,936 | 69,031 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_22_table_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.556,
            0.573,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": "Q. The biggest number in the table is"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.574,
            0.503,
            0.591
          ],
          "content": "Ans. The biggest number in the table is 96,310"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.601,
            0.625,
            0.617
          ],
          "content": "Q. The smallest even number in the table is"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.619,
            0.554,
            0.635
          ],
          "content": "Ans. The smallest even number in the table is 10,396"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.645,
            0.753,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": "Q. The smallest number greater than 50,000 in the table is"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.663,
            0.675,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": "Ans. The smallest number greater than 50,000 in the table is 60,193."
